# Reflection on Writing an Agile Logbook

## Introduction

Writing an Agile Logbook throughout this project was an important part of tracking my progress, organizing my work, and reflecting on what I learned. The purpose of the logbook was to record the tasks I completed, the activities I planned to work on next, and the challenges or risks I encountered during the development of the **SQL Server Health Dashboard**. By updating it regularly, I could monitor my progress and ensure that I remained focused on achieving the project's objectives.

## Learning and Preparation Phase

During September, the logbook helped me track my learning and preparation for the project. I recorded my progress in learning:

- SQL Queries
- Transact-SQL (T-SQL)
- Database Administration
- Backup and Recovery
- Performance Monitoring
- Query Optimization

The logbook also helped me identify areas where I needed additional practice, including:

- Understanding complex joins
- Interpreting execution plans
- Troubleshooting blocking sessions

This allowed me to recognize my weaknesses and plan activities to improve my technical skills.

## Development and Implementation Phase

In October, the logbook became particularly useful as I moved from planning and learning to implementing the **SQL Server Health Dashboard*
